/**
@mainpage CV Inference Platform — Architecture & API Reference

@section intro_sec Overview

The CV Inference Platform is a small, honest distributed system for ingesting
images, running computer-vision inference on them at scale, and serving the
results through a REST API. It is an **event-driven pipeline**, not a
request/response chain: @c ingestion never blocks on inference, and the
@c worker pool scales independently of @c ingestion traffic.

This reference documents the four services and the shared gRPC contract. The
Component Diagram below (@ref components_sec) is the authoritative view of how
the services relate and which contract each boundary speaks — Doxygen's
automatic call/include graphs only see within a single language unit, so the
cross-service topology is described explicitly here.

@section components_sec Component Diagram

Each node is a deployable component; each edge is labelled with the actual
contract that crosses that boundary (HTTP/REST, Redis Stream event, Redis
cache, gRPC, S3 object I/O, or SQL). The image record has a single linear
lifecycle: @c ingestion creates the @c pending row, @c worker enriches it to
@c done / @c failed, and @c results-api only ever reads it.

\dot
digraph cv_inference_platform {
  rankdir=LR;
  fontname="Helvetica";
  node [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10];
  edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9];

  // --- External actor ---
  client [label="client", shape=oval, style=filled, fillcolor="#ffffff"];

  // --- Python services (FastAPI / asyncio) ---
  node [shape=component, style=filled, fillcolor="#cfe8fc"];
  ingestion   [label="ingestion\n(Python / FastAPI)"];
  worker      [label="worker\n(Python / asyncio)"];
  results_api [label="results-api\n(Python / FastAPI)"];

  // --- C++ service ---
  cpp [label="cv-inference-cpp\n(C++ / OpenCV / gRPC)", shape=component,
       style=filled, fillcolor="#ffd9b3"];

  // --- Infrastructure / data stores ---
  redis    [label="Redis\n(Stream broker + cache)", shape=box3d,
            style=filled, fillcolor="#e0e0e0"];
  minio    [label="MinIO (S3)\nraw image bytes", shape=cylinder,
            style=filled, fillcolor="#e0e0e0"];
  postgres [label="PostgreSQL\nimages metadata", shape=cylinder,
            style=filled, fillcolor="#e0e0e0"];

  // --- Contracts (edges) ---
  client      -> ingestion   [label="HTTP/REST\nPOST /images"];
  client      -> results_api [label="HTTP/REST\nGET /images[/{id}]"];

  ingestion   -> minio       [label="S3 put_object\n(raw bytes)"];
  ingestion   -> postgres    [label="SQL INSERT\npending row"];
  ingestion   -> redis       [label="Redis Stream XADD\nimages:uploaded"];

  redis       -> worker      [label="Redis consumer group\nXREADGROUP (workers)"];
  worker      -> minio       [label="S3 get_object\n(raw bytes)"];
  worker      -> cpp         [label="gRPC\nInferImage"];
  worker      -> postgres    [label="SQL upsert\ndone / failed"];

  results_api -> postgres    [label="SQL SELECT\n(read-only)"];
  results_api -> redis       [label="cache-aside\nGET / SET"];
}
\enddot

@section contracts_sec Contract summary

| Boundary                      | Contract                | Direction / purpose                          |
| ----------------------------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| client → ingestion            | HTTP/REST               | Upload an image (`POST /images`)             |
| client → results-api          | HTTP/REST               | Poll / list results (`GET /images[/{id}]`)   |
| ingestion → MinIO             | S3 (`put_object`)       | Store raw image bytes                        |
| ingestion → PostgreSQL        | SQL `INSERT`            | Seed the `pending` metadata row              |
| ingestion → Redis             | Redis Stream `XADD`     | Emit `images:uploaded` event                 |
| Redis → worker                | Redis consumer group    | `XREADGROUP` fan-out across the worker pool  |
| worker → MinIO                | S3 (`get_object`)       | Fetch raw bytes for inference                |
| worker → cv-inference-cpp     | gRPC (`InferImage`)     | Run the CPU-bound inference step             |
| worker → PostgreSQL           | SQL upsert              | Enrich the row to `done` / `failed`          |
| results-api → PostgreSQL      | SQL `SELECT`            | Read-only result lookups / listing           |
| results-api → Redis           | Redis cache (GET/SET)   | Cache-aside response caching                 |

@note Redis is a single deployed instance that plays two logically distinct
roles: the Stream broker for the `images:uploaded` pipeline, and the
cache-aside store for `results-api`. The diagram shows both edges to make that
dual role explicit.

@section layering_sec Clean Architecture layering (Python services)

Each Python service follows the same inward-pointing layering, so it is a
convention rather than a one-off:

- @c domain — entities & value objects, no framework imports
- @c use_cases — application logic, depends only on @c domain
- @c adapters — FastAPI routers, gRPC clients, event consumers (depend inward)
- @c infra — DB sessions, object-storage clients, config

See `docs/design-decisions.md` for the rationale behind the service split, the
gRPC-vs-REST boundary choice, and the retention strategy.
*/
